Thanks @semx, I pushed two fixes on top.

When the section was cleared or written to between two calls, `appendRow()` wrote only the last lines, so the table lost its header. Now the whole table is rendered again in that case.

`render()` on a section now remembers the lines it wrote, so the first `appendRow()` after it also rewrites only what changed. This removes `calculateRowCount()`, which crashed on rowspans and erased the line above vertical tables, horizontal tables, or rows added with `addRow()`.

Tables wider than the terminal still leave a piece of the old border on each append: that comes from `ConsoleSectionOutput::clear()`, fixed in #67099.

